      {
        "id": "p30-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Use the trapezoidal rule with five points to approximate $I=\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\,dx$, expressing your answer in simplest fraction form.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$I\\approx\\dfrac{5323}{6800}$",
          "worked": "Five points are at $x=0,\\frac14,\\frac12,\\frac34,1$, with $h=\\frac14$.\n\nFor $f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}$,\n$$f(0)=1,\\quad f\\left(\\frac14\\right)=\\frac{16}{17},\\quad f\\left(\\frac12\\right)=\\frac45,\\quad f\\left(\\frac34\\right)=\\frac{16}{25},\\quad f(1)=\\frac12.$$\nThe trapezoidal rule gives\n$$\\begin{aligned}I&\\approx\\frac14\\cdot\\frac12\\left[f(0)+2f\\left(\\frac14\\right)+2f\\left(\\frac12\\right)+2f\\left(\\frac34\\right)+f(1)\\right]\\\\&=\\frac18\\left(1+\\frac{32}{17}+\\frac85+\\frac{32}{25}+\\frac12\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{5323}{6800}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the exact value of $I$, and hence show that $\\pi\\approx\\dfrac{5323}{1700}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$I=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$; hence $\\pi\\approx\\dfrac{5323}{1700}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}I&=\\int_0^1\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[\\tan^{-1}x\\right]_0^1\\\\&=\\frac{\\pi}{4}-0\\\\&=\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\\end{aligned}$$\nUsing part (a),\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi}{4}&\\approx\\frac{5323}{6800},\\\\\\pi&\\approx4\\left(\\frac{5323}{6800}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{5323}{1700}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
